# A new chat starts on the model last chosen in its Project (kept by the
# computer, so iPhone and iPad agree), not on the computer's default, and the
# chat's own choice then wins. The owner of the full order
# is this scenario plus the host's record (`create_stores_the_resolved_effort_and_speed`,
# `preparation_retries_one_conversation_without_starting_work`).
# The fixture Project last used Codex Fixture Mini at Low; the computer's
# default is Codex Fixture. A fresh draft is selected by launch argument.
# The chip drops the provider name ("Fixture Mini", not "Codex Fixture Mini").
# Synthetic host; nothing is sent.
launch --fixture subagent-fixture --fixture chat-layout --fixture chat-layout-unsaved --fixture project-provider-switch --fixture fresh-agent-defaults --fixture project-last-model
wait --id project-agent-picker --contains "Fixture Mini" --timeout 30
wait --id new-chat-effort --timeout 10
wait --contains "Low"
shot model-order-project-last
tap --id project-agent-picker
wait --id new-chat-model:gpt-fixture --timeout 10
tap --id new-chat-model:gpt-fixture
wait --id new-chat-model:gpt-fixture --gone --timeout 10
wait --id project-agent-picker --timeout 10
wait --contains "Fixture Mini" --never 1
shot model-order-chat-choice
